DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     Let _a_+_b_*_i denote the complex number _z.

     The ccrreeaall() functions return the real part _a, and the cciimmaagg() functions
     return the imaginary part _b.

     The ccoonnjj() functions return the complex conjugate _a_-_b_*_i.

     The ccpprroojj() functions return the projection onto the Riemann sphere.  If
     _z contains an infinite component, then the result is _∞ _± _0*_i, where the
     (zero) imaginary part of the result has the same sign as _b.  Otherwise,
     the result is _z.

     These functions do not signal any floating point exceptions.

